# 19. Docker HEALTHCHECK

Health checks monitor application health inside containers.

### Dockerfile Example

```dockerfile
FROM nginx:alpine

HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s \
  --timeout=5s \
  --start-period=10s \
  --retries=3 \
  CMD wget -q -O /dev/null http://127.0.0.1/ || exit 1
```

### Build

```bash
docker build -t nginx-health:v1 .
```

### Run

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name health-app \
  -p 8080:80 \
  nginx-health:v1
```

### Check health

```bash
docker ps

docker inspect health-app
```

### Interview Questions

**Q58. What is the difference between running and healthy?**

Running means the main container process is running.

Healthy means the configured health check is passing.

**Q59. Does Docker automatically restart unhealthy containers?**

No. Health checks report status. Restart policies respond to process termination, not merely an unhealthy status.

