# 20. Docker Restart Policies

| Policy | Description |
|---|---|
| no | Do not automatically restart |
| on-failure | Restart after non-zero exit |
| always | Always restart after termination |
| unless-stopped | Restart unless manually stopped |

### Example

```bash
docker run -d \
  --restart unless-stopped \
  --name web \
  nginx
```

### Update existing container

```bash
docker update --restart unless-stopped web
```

### Interview Question

**Q60. Difference between always and unless-stopped?**

Always restarts the container after termination, including after Docker daemon restart.

Unless-stopped respects an explicit manual stop across daemon restarts.

