# 21. Docker Compose Secrets

Secrets allow sensitive values to be mounted into containers as files.

### Example

```yaml
services:
  app:
    image: nginx:alpine
    secrets:
      - db_password

secrets:
  db_password:
    file: ./db_password.txt
```

Secret location inside the container:

```text
/run/secrets/db_password
```

Important: File-backed Compose secrets require appropriate host file permissions and are not equivalent to an enterprise secrets manager.

