## Scenario 16: Deploy a new application version

**Question:** Application version changes from v1 to v2. How will you deploy it without losing data?

### Build new image

```bash
docker build -t myapp:v2 .
```

### Replace container

```bash
docker stop myapp

docker rm myapp

docker run -d \
  --name myapp \
  -p 8080:5000 \
  -v app-data:/data \
  myapp:v2
```

### Rollback

```bash
docker stop myapp

docker rm myapp

docker run -d \
  --name myapp \
  -p 8080:5000 \
  -v app-data:/data \
  myapp:v1
```

Note: This is a basic single-container replacement, not a zero-downtime deployment. Production zero-downtime deployments require multiple instances, load balancing and controlled traffic switching.

